# The backup verifier's build context is the repository root, and its
# Dockerfile COPYs exactly one file from it (the rest comes FROM the backend
# image and the pinned pgvector image). An allow-list, like backend/ and
# frontend/: without it every build sent the whole tree to the daemon —
# node_modules, and any .env lying in it (ADR-123). BuildKit reads this file
# because it sits beside the Dockerfile with the Dockerfile's name.
*
!deploy/backup/backup-verify.sh
